ate of Saxony\",\"Ernst Rüdiger von Starhemberg\",\"Eugene of Savoy\",\"Eunuch\",\"Expedition to Mostaganem (1558)\",\"Fall of Constantinople\",\"Fall of Gallipoli\",\"Fall of Philadelphia\",\"Fall of Tlemcen (1518)\",\"Fedorovych uprising\",\"First Battle of Zrínyiújvár\",\"First Mongol invasion of Poland\",\"First Siege of Missolonghi\",\"First Silesian Uprising\",\"France–Habsburg rivalry\",\"Franconia\",\"Franconian Circle\",\"Frans Geffels\",\"French invasion of Russia\",\"French–German enmity\",\"Galicia–Volhynia Wars\",\"General of the Artillery\",\"Geographic coordinate system\",\"Georg Rimpler\",\"George Ducas\",\"German–Polish War (1003–1018)\",\"German–Polish War (1028–1031)\",\"Ghetto uprisings\",\"Gollub War\",\"Gonzales Franciscus Casteels\",\"Grand Ducal Lithuanian Army\",\"Grand Duchy of Baden\",\"Grand Vizier\",\"Great Northern War\",\"Great Plague of Vienna\",\"Great Siege of Malta\",\"Great Turkish War\",\"Greater Poland uprising (1848)\",\"Greater Poland uprising (1918–1919)\",\"Gunpowder\",\"Győr\",\"Habsburg Spain\",\"Habsburg monarchy\",\"Heiligenstadt, Vienna\",\"Historical drama\",\"History of Poland (1795–1918)\",\"History of Poland (1939–1945)\",\"History of Poland (1945–1989)\",\"History of Poland (1989–present)\",\"History of Poland during World War I\",\"History of Poland during the Jagiellonian dynasty\",\"History of Poland during the Piast dynasty\",\"History of Polish intelligence services\",\"History of Vienna\",\"History of the Polish Army\",\"Holy League (1684)\",\"Holy Name of Mary\",\"Holy Roman Empire\",\"Hungary\",\"Hunger War\",\"ISBN (identifier)\",\"ISSN (identifier)\",\"Imperial Army (Holy Roman Empire)\",\"Imre Thököly\",\"Invasion of Algiers in 1830\",\"Invasion of Poland\",\"Iraq War\",\"Italian campaign (World War II)\",\"James Michener\",\"Jan Matejko\",\"Janissaries\",\"Janissary\",\"Janissary Agha\",\"January Uprising\",\"Jeremy Black (historian)\",\"Jerzy Franciszek Kulczycki\",\"John George III, Elector of Saxony\",\"John III Sobieski\",\"Julius Caesar\",\"Julius Francis, Duke of Saxe-Lauenburg\",\"Juliusz Kossak\",\"Józef Brandt\",\"Kafir\",\"Kahlenberg\",\"Kara Mustafa Pasha\",\"Kazimierz Jan Sapieha\",\"Khan of Crimea\",\"Khmelnytsky Uprising\",\"Kiev offensive (1920)\",\"Killed in action\",\"King of Poland\",\"Kingdom of France\",\"Kingdom of Hungary\",\"Kingdom of Hungary (1526–1867)\",\"Kingdom of Naples\",\"Komárom\",\"Kosiński uprising\",\"Kościuszko Uprising\",\"Kraków\",\"Kunicki's campaign\",\"Kuruc\",\"Kyiv\",\"Kórnica Uprising\",\"Lawrence Wright\",\"Leopold I, Holy Roman Emperor\",\"Leopoldsberg\",\"Leszek Podhorodecki\",\"Linz\",\"Lipka Tatars\",\"List of Ottoman battles in World War I\",\"List of Ottoman battles in the 20th century\",\"List of battles involving the Ottoman Empire\",\"List of cities besieged by the Ottoman Empire\",\"List of military aid to Ukraine during the Russo-Ukrainian War\",\"List of rulers of Moldavia\",\"List of wars involving Poland\",\"List of wars involving the Polish–Lithuanian Commonwealth\",\"Literal translation\",\"Lithuanian Civil War (1432–1438)\",\"Lithuanian–Muscovite War (1534–1537)\",\"Livio Odescalchi\",\"Livonian War\",\"Livonian campaign of Stephen Báthory\",\"Louis William, Margrave of Baden-Baden\",\"Louis XIV\",\"Luigi Ferdinando Marsili\",\"Lwów uprising\",\"Marcin Kątski\",\"Margraviate of Baden\",\"Maximilian II Emanuel, Elector of Bavaria\",\"Maximilian II Emanuel of Bavaria\",\"Mehmed IV\",\"Melvyn Bragg\",\"Michael I Apafi\",\"Miecław's Rebellion\",\"Mihaly Apafi\",\"Mikołaj Hieronim Sieniawski\",\"Military history of Poland during World War II\",\"Military of the Ottoman Empire\",\"Military of the Polish–Lithuanian Commonwealth\",\"Mining (military)\",\"Moldavia\",\"Moldavian Magnate Wars\",\"Moldavian campaign (1497–1499)\",\"Moldavian campaign (1684–1691)\",\"Murad Giray\",\"Muscovite–Lithuanian Wars\",\"Nalyvaiko Uprising\",\"Napoleonic Wars\",\"Nativity of Mary\",\"Naval actions at the siege of Ochakov (1788)\"],\"blacklist\":[],\"lastLinkClicked\":\"Battle of Vienna\"},\"ladderLevel\":0.10267480197739108,\"innerBudgetRemaining\":99.80000000000001,\"probeResult\":{\"pass\":true,\"results\":[]},\"isStable\":false,\"action\":{\"type\":\"NAVIGATE\",\"title\":\"Battle of Abukir (1799)\"},\"next\":{\"currentTitle\":\"Battle of Abukir (1799)\",\"summary\":\"The Battle of Abukir (also known as the Battle of Aboukir or Battle of Abu Qir) was fought on 25 July 1799 between the French Army of the Orient under Napoleon and an Ottoman army under Mustafa Pasha during the French invasion of Egypt and Syria. It is considered the first pitched battle with this name, as there already had been a naval battle on 1 August 1798, the Battle of the Nile. (A second pitched battle followed on 8 March 1801.)\\nNo sooner had the French forces returned from a campaign to Syria, than the Ottoman forces were transported to Egypt by an Anglo-Ottoman fleet under Sidney Smith to put an end to French rule in Egypt. Pasha was an experienced commander who had fought against the Russians. He knew that cavalry charges against the French squares were futile. So, he sought to avoid them by fortifying his beachhead with two defensive lines. From this beachhead Pasha could carry out the invasion of Egypt. However, Napoleon immediately saw the flaw in the tactic as it meant that the Ottomans had nowhere to run if routed.\\nThe French attacked the Ottoman positions and quickly broke through the first defensive line before it was fully completed. The second line, however, proved tougher to defeat and the French withdrew for a while. At this point, cavalry general Murat saw his opportunity and attacked with his cavalry, quickly routing the exposed Ottomans. Murat's charge was so rapid that he burst inside Pasha's tent and captured him, severing two of his fingers with his sabre. In return, Pasha shot Murat in the jaw. Immediately, Murat was operated on and resumed his duties the next day.\\nThe Ottoman army fled in panic. Some Ottomans drowned trying to swim to the British ships two miles away from shore, while others fled to Abukir castle, but they surrendered shortly thereafter. The Ottoman army was annihilated, while French losses were under 1,000. News of the victory reached France before Napoleon arrived in October and this made him even more popular, an important asset considering the troubles brewing in the French Directory. This battle temporarily secured France's control over Egypt.\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle%20of%20Abukir%20(1799)\",\"goal\":\"French Revolution\",\"history\":[\"Battle of Vienna\",\"Battle of Abukir (1799)\"],\"depth\":2,\"links\":[\"Abu Qir\",\"Acre, Israel\",\"Adana campaign\",\"Al-Hasa Expedition 1871\",\"Alexandria\",\"Algiers expedition (1541)\",\"Antoine-Jean Gros\",\"Antoine de Phélippeaux\",\"Arc de Triomphe\",\"Armée d'Orient (1798) order of battle\",\"Auguste de Marmont\",\"Azov campaigns (1695–96)\",\"Barnsley\",\"Battle at Jurjeve Stijene\",\"Battle of Aboukir (Lejeune)\",\"Battle of Abukir (1801)\",\"Battle of Abukir (disambiguation)\",\"Battle of Akhaltsikhe\",\"Battle of Akhaltsikhe (1853)\",\"Battle of Al-Safra\",\"Battle of Al Khankah\",\"Battle of Al Wajbah\",\"Battle of Aladzha\",\"Battle of Alamana\",\"Battle of Alborán\",\"Battle of Albulena\",\"Battle of Alcácer Quibir\",\"Battle of Alexandria (1801)\",\"Battle of Andros (1696)\",\"Battle of Andros (1790)\",\"Battle of Ankara\",\"Battle of Arachova\",\"Battle of Arpachai\",\"Battle of Aspindza\",\"Battle of Athos\",\"Battle of Banja Luka\",\"Battle of Bapheus\",\"Battle of Batin\",\"Battle of Batočina\",\"Battle of Başgedikler\",\"Battle of Beirut (1520)\",\"Battle of Bileća\",\"Battle of Breadfield\",\"Battle of Brest (1592)\",\"Battle of Brest (1596)\",\"Battle of Cape Celidonia\",\"Battle of Cape Corvo\",\"Battle of Cape Kaliakra\",\"Battle of Cecora (1620)\",\"Battle of Chaldiran\",\"Battle of Chelif\",\"Battle of Călugăreni\",\"Battle of Cătlăbuga\