nd Republic\",\"French Sign Language\",\"French Sign Language family\",\"French Third Republic\",\"French Wars of Religion\",\"French West Indies\",\"French adverbs\",\"French alphabet\",\"French architecture\",\"French art\",\"French articles and determiners\",\"French braille\",\"French colonial empire\",\"French conjugation\",\"French criminal law\",\"French cuisine\",\"French fashion\",\"French franc\",\"French government\",\"French grammar\",\"French in France\",\"French language in Cambodia\",\"French language in Canada\",\"French language in Laos\",\"French language in Lebanon\",\"French language in Vietnam\",\"French language in the United States\",\"French literature\",\"French of France\",\"French orthography\",\"French people\",\"French people in India\",\"French personal pronouns\",\"French philosophy\",\"French phonology\",\"French poetry\",\"French pronouns\",\"French verb morphology\",\"French verbs\",\"Frenchville French\",\"Fricative consonant\",\"Friulian language\",\"Front vowel\",\"Fundamental laws of the Kingdom of France\",\"Futunan language\",\"Futur antérieur\",\"Futur simple\",\"Future perfect\",\"Gabon\",\"Galician language\",\"Galician–Asturian\",\"Galician–Portuguese\",\"Gallo-Italic languages\",\"Gallo-Italic of Basilicata\",\"Gallo-Italic of Sicily\",\"Gallo-Romance languages\",\"Gallo language\",\"Gallurese\",\"Gambia\",\"Gardiol language\",\"Gascon dialect\",\"Gatineau\",\"Gaul\",\"Gaulish language\",\"General Conference on Weights and Measures\",\"Genoese dialect\",\"Geographical distribution of French speakers\",\"Geography of France\",\"German Sign Language\",\"German Sign Language family\",\"German language\",\"Germanic languages\",\"Geste de Garin de Monglane\",\"Ghana\",\"Gitxsan language\",\"Glossary of French expressions in English\",\"Glottolog\",\"Government of National Defense\",\"Grammatical aspect\",\"Grammatical case\",\"Grammatical gender\",\"Grammatical genders\",\"Grammatical mood\",\"Grammatical number\",\"Grammatical person\",\"Grammatical tense\",\"Grand Siècle\",\"Grapheme\",\"Grave accent\",\"Great Recession in Europe\",\"Greeks in pre-Roman Gaul\",\"Grenada\",\"Grenadian Creole French\",\"Guadeloupe\",\"Guernésiais\",\"Guianese Creole\",\"Guillemet\",\"Guinea\",\"Guinea-Bissau\",\"Gulf Coast\",\"Gwichʼin language\",\"Haida language\",\"Haisla language\",\"Haiti\",\"Haitian Creole\",\"Haitian French\"],\"blacklist\":[],\"lastLinkClicked\":\"French language\"},\"ladderLevel\":0.24919709262897788,\"innerBudgetRemaining\":99.20000000000005,\"probeResult\":{\"pass\":true,\"results\":[]},\"isStable\":false,\"action\":{\"type\":\"NAVIGATE\",\"title\":\"French Revolution\"},\"next\":{\"currentTitle\":\"French Revolution\",\"summary\":\"The French Revolution was a period of political and societal change in France that began with the Estates General of 1789 and ended with the Coup of 18 Brumaire on 9 November 1799. Many of the revolution's ideas are considered fundamental principles of liberal democracy, and its values remain central to modern French political discourse. It was caused by a combination of social, political, and economic factors which the existing regime proved unable to manage.  \\nFinancial crisis and widespread social distress led to the convocation of the Estates General in May 1789, its first meeting since 1614. The representatives of the Third Estate broke away and re-constituted themselves as a National Assembly in June. The Storming of the Bastille in Paris on 14 July led to a series of radical measures by the Assembly, including the abolition of feudalism, state control over the Catholic Church in France, and issuing the Declaration of the Rights of Man and of the Citizen. \\nThe next three years were dominated by a struggle for political control. King Louis XVI's attempted flight to Varennes in June 1791 further discredited the monarchy, and military defeats after the outbreak of the French Revolutionary Wars in April 1792 led to the insurrection of 10 August 1792. As a result, the monarchy was replaced by the French First Republic in September, followed by the execution of Louis XVI himself in January 1793.\\nAfter another revolt in June 1793, the constitution was suspended, and political power passed from the National Convention to the Committee of Public Safety, dominated by radical Jacobins led by Maximilien Robespierre. About 16,000 people were sentenced by the Revolutionary Tribunal and executed in the Reign of Terror, which ended in July 1794 with the Thermidorian Reaction. Weakened by external threats and internal opposition, the Committee of Public Safety was replaced in November 1795 by the Directory. Its instability ended in 1799 with the coup of 18 Brumaire and the establishment of the Consulate, with Napoleon Bonaparte as First Consul.\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French%20Revolution\",\"goal\":\"French Revolution\",\"history\":[\"Battle of Vienna\",\"Battle of Abukir (1799)\",\"Battle of Aboukir (Lejeune)\",\"Entry of Charles X into Paris After His Coronation\",\"French language\",\"French Revolution\"],\"depth\":6,\"links\":[\"11 September 1922 Revolution\",\"13 Vendémiaire\",\"14 July Revolution\",\"1791 French legislative election\",\"1792 French National Convention election\",\"1795 French legislative election\",\"1798 French legislative election\",\"1851 French coup d'état\",\"18 Brumaire\",\"1911 Revolution\",\"1935 Greek coup d'état attempt\",\"1946 Italian institutional referendum\",\"1952 Egyptian revolution\",\"1960 South African republic referendum\",\"1969 Libyan coup d'état\",\"1970 Cambodian coup d'état\",\"1987 Fijian coups d'état\",\"2005 French riots\",\"2010 Kyrgyz Revolution\",\"2011 Egyptian revolution\",\"2017 French presidential election\",\"2021 French labor protests\",\"2022 French presidential election\",\"2022 Russian invasion of Ukraine\",\"5 October 1910 revolution\",\"A Discourse on the Love of Our Country\",\"A Vindication of the Rights of Men\",\"Abolition of feudalism in France\",\"Abolition of monarchy\",\"Abortion in France\",\"Abraham Lincoln\",\"Absolute monarchy\",\"Absolute monarchy in France\",\"Action of 13 January 1797\",\"Action of 25 January 1797\",\"Active citizenship\",\"Acts of the Apostles\",\"Adam Philippe, Comte de Custine\",\"Administrative divisions of France\",\"Adolphe Thiers\",\"Adrien Duport\",\"Affair of the Diamond Necklace\",\"Age of Discovery\",\"Age of Enlightenment\",\"Age of Revolution\",\"Agrarian reform\",\"Albert Soboul\",\"Alexander Korsakov\",\"Alexander Suvorov\",\"Alexandre-Théodore-Victor, comte de Lameth\",\"Alexandre Lameth\",\"Alexandre de Beauharnais\",\"Alexis de Tocqueville\",\"Alfred Cobban\",\"Algeciras campaign\",\"Algerian War\",\"Algernon Sidney\",\"American Economic Review\",\"American Revolution\",\"Americas\",\"Anacharsis Cloots\",\"Ancien Régime\",\"Ancien Régime in France\",\"Ancien régime\",\"Ancient history\",\"Andrei Rosenberg\",\"André Chénier\",\"André Masséna\",\"André Rigaud\",\"Andrés Bello\",\"Andy Slaughter\",\"Anglo-French War (1778–1783)\",\"Ann McKechin\",\"Années folles\",\"Ante-Nicene period\",\"Anti-bureaucratic revolution\",\"Anti-clericalism\",\"Anti-corruption\",\"Anti-monarchism in Japan\",\"Antoine-François Momoro\",\"Antoine Barnave\",\"Antoine Christophe Merlin\",\"Antoine Christophe Saliceti\",\"Antoine Lavoisier\",\"Antoine Pierre Joseph Marie Barnave\",\"Antoine Quentin Fouquier-Tinville\",\"Antonio Ricardos\",\"Apostles in the New Testament\",\"Apostolic Age\",\"Apostolic Fathers\",\"Arab Spring\",\"Archbasilica of Saint John Lateran\",\"Archduke Charles, Duke of Teschen\",\"Argentine Revolution\",\"Arian controversy\",\"Armoire de fer\",\"Army of Italy (France)\",\"Arnaud II de La Porte\",\"Art of Europe\",\"Assembly of Notables\",\"Assembly of Vizille\",\"Assignats\",\"Assumption of Mary\",\"Atheist\",\"Atlantic Revolutions\",\"August Decrees\",\"August Revolution\",\"Auguste de Marmont\",\"Augustin Robespierre\",\"Austrian Empire\",\"Austr